## Interface: 16001, 120100, 120000, 120005, 110200
# FIRST is the target: Forever, Mainline, interface 16001 (docs/07).
# The rest let the same files load on a live retail client for testing --
# retail is Mainline too, so it verifies the API surface without being
# Forever. Every result from retail must still be re-confirmed on the beta.
## Title: Forever Hearthstone
## Notes: A faithful recreation of Hearthstone's Basic, Classic, Naxxramas and Goblins vs Gnomes sets, played between two players sitting near each other in the world.
## Author: bbwfan85
## Version: 1.0.4
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\ForeverHearthstone\Art\minimap-icon.tga
## AddonCompartmentFunc: ForeverHearthstone_OnAddonCompartmentClick
## SavedVariables: ForeverHearthstoneDB
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: ForeverHearthstoneCharDB
## X-Patch-Pin: 7234 (Basic + Classic + Naxxramas + Goblins vs Gnomes)

# LOAD ORDER MATTERS.
#
# Each file captures its dependencies into locals at load time -- Ops.lua does
# `local Selector = ns.Selector` -- so a file must never load before what it
# captures. This order is the same one tests/harness.lua uses, and the test
# suite is what proves it is correct: the engine loads and runs headless under
# plain Lua 5.1 with nothing stubbed.
#
# Engine/ imports ZERO WoW API. So do Client/Assets, Client/FX, Client/UI/Layout
# and Client/Controller. Only Client/UI/Board.lua and Client/Main.lua touch the
# platform. That rule is what let this project survive discovering that the
# brief's "Forever uses the Classic API" premise was wrong -- see docs/07.

